---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

import '../assets/brand/tokens.css';
import '../styles/site.css';
import heroWide from '../assets/brand/diagrams/gate-hero.svg?raw';
import heroNarrow from '../assets/brand/diagrams/gate-hero-narrow.svg?raw';

const title = 'Waggle: when contributors run agents, the agents collide';
const description =
  'Several people, each running an AI coding agent, means overlapping edits, duplicated work, and conflicting pull requests. Waggle gives each task a claim and a GitHub check that blocks a merge outside it. A person stays in control.';
const site = import.meta.env.SITE;
const canonical = site ? new URL('/', site).href : undefined;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    {canonical && <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />}
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
  </head>
  <body class="lp">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
      <nav class="lp-nav" aria-label="Main">
        <a class="mark" href="/">Waggle</a>
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/docs/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
        <a href="/docs/gate/">Gate</a>
        <a href="/docs/claims-and-leases/">Claims</a>
        <a href="/docs/config/">Config</a>
        <a href="/docs/cli/">CLI</a>
        <a href="/docs/recipes/">Recipes</a>
      </nav>

      <header class="lp-hero">
        <h1>When contributors run agents, the agents collide.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Overlapping edits, the same work done twice, pull requests that conflict, and nobody who can say who is on what.
          Waggle gives each task a lane and fails a merge that leaves it. A person writes the lane and stays in control.
        </p>
        <div class="lp-actions">
          <a class="lp-btn primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="lp-btn" href="/docs/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <figure class="lp-diagram" style="margin-inline: 0">
        <div class="wide" set:html={heroWide} />
        <div class="narrow" set:html={heroNarrow} />
      </figure>

      <section aria-labelledby="pains">
        <h2 id="pains">What goes wrong today</h2>
        <div class="lp-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Overlapping edits</h3>
            <p>Two agents change the same files. One overwrites the other, or the pull requests will not merge.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>The same work, twice</h3>
            <p>Nothing records that a task is already taken, so a second agent starts it.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Nobody can see who is on what</h3>
            <p>Branches pile up. A person has to reconstruct the plan from the diff.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="fix">
        <h2 id="fix">How Waggle fixes it</h2>
        <div class="lp-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>A claim</h3>
            <p>
              A record a person writes before the work starts. It names the task, the directories that task may change, and
              the branches its pull request may come from. The agent does not write it.
              <a href="/docs/claims-and-leases/">Claims and leases</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>A lease</h3>
            <p>Those directories. That is the lane the agent is supposed to stay inside.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>The gate</h3>
            <p>
              A GitHub merge check. It fails a pull request whose commits change a path outside the lease, or whose claim
              does not name that pull request's branch. It checks every commit, not only the final diff.
              <a href="/docs/gate/">The gate spec</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>A Keeper stays in control</h3>
            <p>
              A Keeper is a person on the approver list. Paths you list as protected still need that person's approval.
              Control files such as workflows fail no matter what the claim says. Waggle does not run the agents.
              <a href="/docs/gate/#5-risk-tiers-and-protected-paths">Protected paths</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="who">
        <h2 id="who">Who it's for</h2>
        <p>
          Teams, and open-source projects, where more than one contributor uses an AI coding agent on the same repository.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="lp-limits">
      <div class="lp-wrap">
        <h2>What it does not do</h2>
        <p>
          It does not schedule or run agents, and it is not a sandbox. It binds only on PRs that must pass the check, an
          admin bypass merges without it, and the required check can be forged by a workflow or token with the right
          permissions. The limits are written down, with the tests that show them, in
          <a href="/docs/gate/#10-limits-and-known-bypasses">the gate spec</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Waggle is pre-1.0 and supports GitHub only. The spec describes what the code does today, and the recipes have not
          been run end to end with each tool.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="lp-wrap lp-foot">
      <p><a href="/docs/why-waggle/">Why Waggle: questions from teams</a></p>
      <p>The <code>waggle</code> CLI is Apache-2.0. The templates <code>waggle init</code> writes into your repo are MIT-0.</p>
      <p>Copyright 2026 Level 19 Enterprises, LLC.</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
